invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_scalar.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_scalar
reason: exponent_low_nibble shifts its position by 3 where the limb index
  is the position over 16, so positions 16 to 31 read EXPONENT_LOW[2] and
  [3], past the two limbs the array holds.
  proof/p256_wide_scalar_harness.c proves that read in bounds for every
  position the inverse's loop passes. Each run is a proof, so this
  belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
    return (EXPONENT_LOW[at >> 4] >> (4 * (at & 15))) & 15U;
--- new
    return (EXPONENT_LOW[at >> 3] >> (4 * (at & 15))) & 15U;
